legal.rules:
These rules apply to everything shown on {site}: pictures, drawings, texts, titles, names and links. A person checks all content before it is published. By ordering, you confirm that your content follows these rules.

## Not allowed
- anything illegal;
- nudity, pornography and sexual content;
- violence, blood, and weapons in an aggressive context;
- hate, extremist symbols, bullying and harassment;
- personal data or photos of other people without their consent;
- scams, phishing, malware, pyramid schemes and gambling without a licence;
- logos, characters and other content you do not have the rights to;
- political advertising;
- links to websites with such content.

## Technical limits
All pixels form one still picture: animations and videos are not possible. Links must start with http:// or https://. We may refuse content that cannot be read at its size or that pretends to be part of the website (for example fake buttons).

## When content breaks the rules
- Before approval we reject the content and tell you why. You can send different content within {days, plural, one {# day} other {# days}}; otherwise we refund the whole payment.
- After approval we can hide content at once and remove it for good if it breaks these rules or the law. Removed content is not refunded (see the [terms of service](/terms)). You always get an e-mail with the reasons.
- You can object to any decision: reply to our e-mail or write to {email}. A person looks at it again.

## Reporting
Anyone can report content with the “Report” button in the window of each spot or on the [Report content](/report) page. We confirm every report and tell the reporter what we decided.
